## 4. Prohibited Commercial Redistribution

Without a separate written license from the Licensor, You may not:

a. sell, rent, lease, sublicense, commercially license, or otherwise commercially distribute the Software itself as a Standalone Codec Product;

b. sell, rent, lease, sublicense, commercially license, or otherwise commercially distribute a Modified Version as a Standalone Codec Product;

c. rebrand, rename, fork, port, wrap, or modify the Software and commercially offer the resulting product where its primary purpose or commercial value remains substantially equivalent to LX-VOXEL;

d. offer the Software or a Modified Version as a paid codec SDK, codec library, codec API, encoding or decoding service, transcoding service, or substantially equivalent commercial offering;

e. charge customers primarily for access to the Software or its codec functionality;

f. use cosmetic, organizational, interface-level, build-system, or minor technical modifications to circumvent the restrictions of this Section.

The restrictions in this Section do not prohibit charging money for an Integrated Product merely because that Integrated Product contains or uses LX-VOXEL.

For example, subject to the other terms of this License, LX-VOXEL may be incorporated into and distributed with a commercial game, media player, audio workstation, operating system, hardware device, streaming application, editing application, or other substantially broader product.

